meta {
  name: 01. BEFORE - Search Regex Syntax Crash (500 Error)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: http://localhost:5050/api/stories?search=([a-z]+
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  search: ([a-z]+
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # VULN-02: Regular Expression Query Injection & Syntax Crash
  
  ## Objective:
  Demonstrate that unescaped regex characters passed in the `search` query parameter cause an unhandled MongoDB/V8 regex compilation error, resulting in an internal server crash (HTTP 500).
  
  ## How to test:
  1. Ensure you have logged in and `{{token}}` is populated.
  2. Send the request.
  3. Observe the HTTP 500 Internal Server Error leaking `SyntaxError: Invalid regular expression`.
  4. Capture a screenshot for your BEFORE evidence!
}
